1
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:19,060
The first need is my Stand.

2
00:00:19,978 --> 00:00:21,479
My Stand, The World,

3
00:00:21,563 --> 00:00:28,361
and what lies beyond it are
the path for men to advance further.

4
00:00:29,779 --> 00:00:33,324
My second need is a trustworthy friend.

5
00:00:33,908 --> 00:00:37,662
He must be someone
who can control his desires.

6
00:00:38,288 --> 00:00:41,624
The desire for power, fame, money, sex…

7
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:43,418
He must be free of those things.

8
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:48,923
It must be someone who chooses
God's laws over the laws of men.

9
00:00:50,258 --> 00:00:54,763
Will I, Dio, ever meet
someone with this character trait?

10
00:00:55,889 --> 00:01:01,895
I also need
at least 36 souls of the worst convicts.

11
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:06,483
Souls of sinners have tremendous energy.

12
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:11,654
I need 14 words.

13
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:14,074
To prevent ever forgetting these words,

14
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:19,454
I will etch them onto my Stand itself.

15
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:23,625
I also need courage.

16
00:01:24,417 --> 00:01:28,338
I must have the courage to
let go of my Stand just once.

17
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:31,549
My decaying Stand

18
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:35,178
will gather and absorb
the souls of 36 convicts.

19
00:01:35,261 --> 00:01:38,306
It will then give birth to something new.

20
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:41,017
The spawned creature will awaken.

21
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:49,901
It will be curious about the 14 words
spoken by the trusted friend.

22
00:01:55,615 --> 00:02:00,453
My friend will find me trustworthy
and he will consider me his friend.

23
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:04,249
Finally, I need the location.

24
00:02:04,874 --> 00:02:08,253
It will be north latitude,
28 degrees 24 minutes,

25
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:11,631
west longitude, 80 degrees 36 minutes.

26
00:02:17,095 --> 00:02:20,098
Wait for the next new moon.

27
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:25,103
Heaven will appear then.

28
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:30,275
Good morning, Father.

29
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:31,901
You've grown your hair out.

30
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:35,071
When was the last time
you returned home to the mainland?

31
00:02:36,614 --> 00:02:38,992
I have no use for this place now.

32
00:02:42,287 --> 00:02:46,332
The birthed creature now belongs to me.

33
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:56,175
The only thing left to do is
to wait for the time of heaven.

34
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:33,231
EPISODE 23: LOCK OF THE JAIL!

35
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:36,943
DISCIPLINARY WING

36
00:04:47,412 --> 00:04:48,746
This is the worst!

37
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,331
How do I get out of this one?

38
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:53,334
This is the highest
maximum security measure ever.

39
00:04:53,418 --> 00:04:55,420
All the guards have guns too.

40
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:57,839
It's too dangerous to be here
with all the guards,

41
00:04:57,922 --> 00:04:59,424
even for just another minute.

42
00:05:00,925 --> 00:05:03,052
Hey, Jolyne, can you hear me?

43
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:04,053
Are you listening?

44
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:06,681
The priest isn't on this island anymore.

45
00:05:06,764 --> 00:05:09,600
He already left Green Dolphin Street.

46
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:12,270
He didn't take anything, though.

47
00:05:12,353 --> 00:05:15,398
He wasn't carrying a baby with him!

48
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:19,694
It's too boring in here.
I even pierced my own belly button.

49
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:26,034
Do you have my father's disc, Emporio?
You got it now?

50
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:29,037
Did you get in contact
with the Speedwagon Foundation?

51
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:31,831
I can't. The security is too tight
right now.

52
00:05:31,914 --> 00:05:34,042
I have the disc though, Jolyne.

53
00:05:34,125 --> 00:05:36,627
I wouldn't put it down. Never.

54
00:05:37,211 --> 00:05:39,464
Good. Well, I'm getting out of here.

55
00:05:39,547 --> 00:05:41,549
- Lead the way.
- Jolyne.

56
00:05:41,632 --> 00:05:43,176
The prison workers think

57
00:05:43,259 --> 00:05:45,762
that you are the sole survivor from
the Disciplinary Wing.

58
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:47,764
Though they can't pin it on you,

59
00:05:47,847 --> 00:05:50,808
you are the only person
they can question right now.

60
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:53,644
That's why this cell is
under strict observation.

61
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:56,814
Do you want to leave the cell
and come to my room?

62
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:58,733
No, Emporio.

63
00:05:58,816 --> 00:06:02,236
By leave, I mean
getting out of this shitty prison.

64
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,572
I don't have any more time to waste.

65
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:08,451
I'm breaking out
of the Green Dolphin Island.

66
00:06:08,534 --> 00:06:10,369
Show me the fastest way out of here.

67
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:14,499
I promise I'll contact
the Speedwagon Foundation.

68
00:06:14,582 --> 00:06:17,001
I'll even do that today.

69
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:19,128
Wrong again, Emporio.

70
00:06:19,212 --> 00:06:24,133
This problem is much bigger than
retrieving my father's disc now.

71
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:28,888
If F.F. were alive, they would be
going after that priest as we speak.

72
00:06:28,971 --> 00:06:31,933
And now that I read my father's memory,

73
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:34,477
I understand what Pucchi meant
by 20 years.

74
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:39,065
I now understand why my father
had to seal Dio's ability.

75
00:06:39,148 --> 00:06:42,735
My father would never let
the priest get away.

76
00:06:42,819 --> 00:06:44,987
And I am Jolyne Cujoh!

77
00:06:45,071 --> 00:06:48,199
I have to seal what he has obtained again!

78
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:53,579
Emporio.

79
00:06:54,163 --> 00:06:56,582
Do you plan to stay here
for the rest of your life?

80
00:06:56,666 --> 00:06:59,669
It's up to you,
but I want you to come with me.

81
00:07:00,169 --> 00:07:02,004
You don't understand, Jolyne.

82
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:03,506
You don't get it at all.

83
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:05,341
But I do.

84
00:07:05,424 --> 00:07:08,886
I can break out of these bars
in three minutes.

85
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:10,179
But what about after that?

86
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:14,308
No one is left to help you.

87
00:07:14,392 --> 00:07:16,227
Ermes, Anastasia…

88
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:18,771
They are still under treatment
at the medical wing.

89
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:22,066
For some reason, Weather Forecast
has been holed up in his own room.

90
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:24,110
He won't even come visit my room.

91
00:07:24,193 --> 00:07:27,447
I can leave through
the Ultra Security House Unit.

92
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:28,698
We got to the wetlands.

93
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:29,740
We can't.

94
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:32,952
No jailbreak attempt has ever succeeded.

95
00:07:33,035 --> 00:07:36,330
Some prisoners were detained
for even contemplating a breakout.

96
00:07:36,831 --> 00:07:39,834
Anyway, unless you can stop time
like your father,

97
00:07:39,917 --> 00:07:42,670
no one can ever leave this prison.

98
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:46,716
I don't know what,
but there's something about this place.

99
00:07:46,799 --> 00:07:49,010
Something more than surveillance cameras,

100
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:52,305
as if the prison itself was
a guard with a mind of its own.

101
00:07:52,388 --> 00:07:55,892
Emporio, when is the next new moon?

102
00:07:55,975 --> 00:07:57,143
Jolyne,

103
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:59,645
please, just wait for
the Speedwagon Foundation.

104
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:03,107
If we risk it, we might even
lose this disc we finally retrieved!

105
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:05,651
North latitude, 28 degrees 24 minutes.

106
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:07,737
West longitude, 80 degrees 36 minutes.

107
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:08,821
Where is that?

108
00:08:09,864 --> 00:08:12,200
J-Jolyne…

109
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:14,160
I can't help you with this.

110
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:35,932
I have a message from Pale Snake.

111
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:38,267
Everything is over.

112
00:08:38,351 --> 00:08:40,603
Don't try to leave this prison.

113
00:08:41,145 --> 00:08:45,483
If you stay here, we won't get in the way
of you delivering the disc to Jotaro.

114
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:57,036
You've got guts, I'll give you that.

115
00:08:57,119 --> 00:08:59,664
You showed me your face and your Stand.

116
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:01,040
And what's your name?

117
00:09:01,582 --> 00:09:03,042
I am Mew Mew.

118
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:05,795
My Stand is called Jailhouse Lock.

119
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:08,756
I'm showing it to you as a warning.

120
00:09:08,839 --> 00:09:12,593
Did he order you to finish me off?

121
00:09:12,677 --> 00:09:15,471
If your plans are to break out
of this jail, then yes.

122
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:17,807
My plans?

123
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:19,392
No, I don't have any plans.

124
00:09:20,184 --> 00:09:21,185
I'm leaving now!

125
00:09:27,858 --> 00:09:29,235
Her Stand is in the bars!

126
00:09:29,318 --> 00:09:32,697
I'll say it one more time, Jolyne Cujoh.

127
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,657
Don't touch the bars.

128
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:38,202
The more you think about escaping,
the closer you'll be to your death.

129
00:09:38,286 --> 00:09:40,371
So this is what your ability does.

130
00:09:40,454 --> 00:09:41,497
Take this!

131
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:44,500
What?

132
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:49,505
Do you need me to get someone?

133
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:57,096
Are you okay, Jolyne?

134
00:09:57,179 --> 00:10:00,308
Where am I? Why am I here?

135
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:01,809
It's you, Gwess.

136
00:10:01,892 --> 00:10:03,394
Am I in the female wing?

137
00:10:04,228 --> 00:10:05,813
It hurts!

138
00:10:08,232 --> 00:10:10,776
"One, grab a pen as soon as you can."

139
00:10:15,323 --> 00:10:20,036
"Two, you can only retain up to
three new pieces of information."

140
00:10:20,119 --> 00:10:22,997
"Three, defeat the User."

141
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,874
"Her name is Mew Mew."

142
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:30,212
What are these writings
and who wrote them?

143
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:34,091
Did someone write these
while I was asleep?

144
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:35,718
4. GO SEE EMPORIO

145
00:10:35,801 --> 00:10:37,803
Oh, that's right.

146
00:10:37,887 --> 00:10:40,806
I was locked up because of what happened
at the Ultra Security House Unit.

147
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:42,600
I gave myself a belly piercing.

148
00:10:42,683 --> 00:10:44,894
Then, I ran into Emporio.

149
00:10:45,394 --> 00:10:49,315
I told him I'm getting out of here
to go after the priest.

150
00:10:49,398 --> 00:10:50,775
And then, after that…

151
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:52,777
After that…

152
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:54,403
I…

153
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:55,905
What?

154
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:58,491
After I said I was leaving,
I remember someone coming.

155
00:10:58,574 --> 00:11:01,619
But who was it?

156
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:07,541
This is my handwriting. Did I write these?

157
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:11,420
No way. When did I write them, though?
I don't even remember writing them.

158
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:14,757
Tell me, why am I back here
in the female wing?

159
00:11:17,551 --> 00:11:19,762
Hey! Answer me!

160
00:11:19,845 --> 00:11:21,806
Why are you ignoring me?

161
00:11:21,889 --> 00:11:24,141
I must've been sleeping
since I don't remember.

162
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:26,185
I'm serious!

163
00:11:26,268 --> 00:11:29,939
Oh, also, do you have a pen?

164
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:31,732
I need a pen. Give me one.

165
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:41,492
Hey, you…

166
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:43,702
I'm really serious.

167
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:46,622
Do you think I wrote these on myself?

168
00:11:47,164 --> 00:11:48,749
That I wrote on my own body?

169
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:54,171
2. YOU CAN ONLY RETAIN UP TO
THREE NEW PIECES OF INFORMATION

170
00:11:56,215 --> 00:11:58,509
Hey, Gwess… be honest.

171
00:11:59,176 --> 00:12:02,763
Have I been asking you the same question
over and over again?

172
00:12:04,765 --> 00:12:06,559
Can you do me a favor?

173
00:12:07,351 --> 00:12:11,814
Can you tell me
all the things I've asked you already?

174
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:21,240
"Jolyne, the prison doctor
has diagnosed you

175
00:12:21,323 --> 00:12:23,993
with temporary amnesia brought on

176
00:12:24,076 --> 00:12:26,829
by a great shock you received
while in the Hole."

177
00:12:26,912 --> 00:12:31,292
"You can only memorize
up to three things at a time."

178
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:34,086
"You can still remember the past,

179
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:37,548
but if you memorize a fourth new thing,
you will forget one."

180
00:12:37,631 --> 00:12:40,843
"However, since this will not affect
your life as a prisoner,

181
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:44,305
you were sent back
to the female wing two days ago."

182
00:12:44,805 --> 00:12:45,931
Two days?

183
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:47,975
I've been here that long?

184
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:50,644
Get better soon, Jolyne.

185
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:52,146
For two days…

186
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:55,816
Have I been repeating the same questions
for two whole days?

187
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:57,651
But why?

188
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,488
"Defeat the User."

189
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:02,114
"Her name is Mew Mew."

190
00:13:02,781 --> 00:13:04,533
This is…

191
00:13:05,117 --> 00:13:07,286
Could this be… No, it can't be…

192
00:13:07,369 --> 00:13:09,121
It's a Stand ability!

193
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:11,373
They're trying to keep me
locked up in here!

194
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:13,709
I'm under attack!

195
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:15,878
I remember seeing Emporio.

196
00:13:16,587 --> 00:13:17,838
And then…

197
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:20,674
After that…

198
00:13:20,758 --> 00:13:21,842
After that…

199
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:24,803
Let's see… I remember something happening.

200
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:33,062
WASH YOUR HANDS
DON'T FORGET TO WEAR YOUR PANTIES

201
00:13:37,024 --> 00:13:38,317
Shit!

202
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,653
What the hell?

203
00:13:42,655 --> 00:13:44,240
By the way, Gwess,

204
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:46,867
do you know anyone named Mew Mew?

205
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:49,537
You haven't asked that yet, Jolyne.

206
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,247
Her prisoner cell is upstairs.

207
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:53,999
I think she has ratty, blond hair.

208
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:55,376
She's about your height.

209
00:13:55,459 --> 00:14:00,756
I don't know why she's here,
but I bet she was whoring around.

210
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:03,592
Where do I go to see her?

211
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:06,095
She was here until a moment ago, Jolyne.

212
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:08,305
She just walked by.

213
00:14:15,688 --> 00:14:18,732
Can you tell me how she looks like again?

214
00:14:18,816 --> 00:14:21,443
She's about 175cm.

215
00:14:21,527 --> 00:14:24,572
Her hair is platinum blonde
and it's ratty.

216
00:14:24,655 --> 00:14:26,282
She wears fishnets.

217
00:14:27,449 --> 00:14:29,285
This is the female wing.

218
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:31,537
How did I get back here?

219
00:14:35,374 --> 00:14:37,251
Who's Mew Mew?

220
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:38,335
What's the matter?

221
00:14:38,836 --> 00:14:40,170
No…

222
00:14:40,254 --> 00:14:42,381
You just said you wanted lunch.

223
00:14:42,464 --> 00:14:44,466
It's almost lunchtime.

224
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:45,926
Is that right?

225
00:14:49,221 --> 00:14:51,724
Don't think about getting out of here,
Jolyne Cujoh.

226
00:14:52,224 --> 00:14:58,564
You can't attack me
and my Jailhouse Lock, ever.

227
00:15:03,235 --> 00:15:04,904
STAND NAME: STONE OCEAN
STAND MASTER: JOLYNE CUJOH

228
00:15:10,534 --> 00:15:13,537
Pale Snake was the priest.

229
00:15:14,872 --> 00:15:16,665
F.F. figured it out for us.

230
00:15:19,585 --> 00:15:20,669
And then….

231
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:24,548
They died, didn't they?

232
00:15:40,898 --> 00:15:42,566
Bottoms up.

233
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:50,157
I'll avenge you.

234
00:15:51,825 --> 00:15:54,119
Hey! Why are you grabbing food?

235
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:55,663
Give me your ticket first.

236
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:57,873
I'm here to grab the packed lunch.

237
00:15:57,957 --> 00:15:59,959
Like I said, ticket first.

238
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:02,795
You won't be sneaking one away.

239
00:16:02,878 --> 00:16:05,381
Now show it to me. Stop taking forever.

240
00:16:05,464 --> 00:16:06,966
If you don't have it, then leave.

241
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:09,134
Now scram.

242
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:10,177
Next.

243
00:16:12,179 --> 00:16:14,306
Did I leave it next to my bed?

244
00:16:14,932 --> 00:16:17,267
I've got to write it somewhere
so I don't forget it.

245
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:20,479
LEAVE FOOD TICKET IN HERE

246
00:16:21,605 --> 00:16:22,439
What?

247
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:27,736
Why am I here again?

248
00:16:28,237 --> 00:16:31,699
Oh, why did I come back up here?

249
00:16:33,951 --> 00:16:36,120
I can't remember a thing.

250
00:16:38,163 --> 00:16:40,499
Why did I come back up here?

251
00:16:40,582 --> 00:16:44,128
Hey Jolyne, that's my lunch!

252
00:16:44,211 --> 00:16:46,255
You ate a good bit of it!

253
00:16:46,338 --> 00:16:48,757
You ate my favorite cheese penne!

254
00:16:48,841 --> 00:16:52,386
You left your ticket
in your pocket, remember?

255
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:57,933
Sorry.

256
00:16:58,017 --> 00:17:00,811
I'll get you another one with my ticket.

257
00:17:00,894 --> 00:17:03,063
No, it's fine. Just stop.

258
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:05,858
I can get it, just give me your ticket.

259
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:12,406
Can you write it down somewhere
that I have your ticket?

260
00:17:12,489 --> 00:17:13,782
Oh, sorry.

261
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:19,496
I GAVE MY FOOD TICKET TO GWESS

262
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:23,292
What's this, a User?
Is it referring to a Stand?

263
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:27,129
Oh, that's right.
I have to go see Emporio.

264
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:30,215
I tried to break out
of the confinement cell.

265
00:17:31,008 --> 00:17:34,845
Emporio must have been with me then.

266
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:38,098
Emporio might know something.

267
00:17:38,182 --> 00:17:39,725
And I need to get out of here.

268
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:41,602
I GAVE MY FOOD TICKET TO GWESS

269
00:17:41,685 --> 00:17:44,730
Hey, I said the mustard's out!

270
00:17:44,813 --> 00:17:47,691
There's not a squeeze left in here.
Do you have another bottle?

271
00:17:50,402 --> 00:17:53,947
Why does it feel like
I'm always eating the same food?

272
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:58,535
I don't have an appetite.
I'll just eat the cheese penne.

273
00:17:58,619 --> 00:18:01,080
Can I sit with you, Jolyne?

274
00:18:08,587 --> 00:18:10,214
I'm sitting down here.

275
00:18:11,006 --> 00:18:13,842
I stepped on a cockroach earlier.

276
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:15,677
It was so gross.

277
00:18:16,261 --> 00:18:20,432
Who is she? She seems to know me.

278
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:22,267
Blonde…

279
00:18:22,351 --> 00:18:23,685
Ratty hair…

280
00:18:23,769 --> 00:18:25,062
Fishnet tights.

281
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:29,358
What the hell did you do that for?

282
00:18:29,942 --> 00:18:31,068
Do you want mustard?

283
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:35,280
What about ketchup?

284
00:18:37,324 --> 00:18:39,701
You aren't fond of dressing, are you?

285
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:50,170
It's pretty good.

286
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:52,339
Thanks.

287
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:55,175
By the way, what's your name?

288
00:18:55,259 --> 00:18:56,218
Oh, no.

289
00:18:56,301 --> 00:18:57,803
I'm so sorry,

290
00:18:57,886 --> 00:19:00,180
I spilled it on you! Let's get you clean.

291
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:04,560
Your arm got drenched.
We need to go clean it off.

292
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:05,644
Take that jacket off.

293
00:19:05,727 --> 00:19:07,604
2. YOU CAN ONLY RETAIN UP TO
THREE NEW PIECES OF INFORMATION

294
00:19:07,688 --> 00:19:10,482
Oh, that's so much better.
There, all squeaky clean!

295
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:12,901
Let's check your pocket too.

296
00:19:17,447 --> 00:19:19,825
That's a gift from me.

297
00:19:19,908 --> 00:19:22,202
Jailhouse Lock.

298
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:26,039
Anyone who touches the cell bars
with my Stand in it to try and escape

299
00:19:26,123 --> 00:19:29,209
can then only remember
three pieces of information.

300
00:19:29,877 --> 00:19:32,546
Their life is then restricted
by the three memories.

301
00:19:32,629 --> 00:19:35,674
It's worse than not having
any memories at all.

302
00:19:36,425 --> 00:19:39,553
They experience over and over again

303
00:19:39,636 --> 00:19:42,472
that everything they do is meaningless.

304
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:45,934
Eventually, this cycle of failure
becomes etched in their bodies.

305
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:50,022
They then lose all drive to escape.

306
00:19:50,105 --> 00:19:52,357
You can even say that they are crippled.

307
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:56,820
This is what you get
for trying to break out.

308
00:20:01,283 --> 00:20:03,035
What do I need to do?

309
00:20:03,118 --> 00:20:04,536
What's important to me?

310
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:06,622
What shouldn't I forget?

311
00:20:06,705 --> 00:20:12,377
That's all I need to get out of this trap.
I just need one thing!

312
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:14,588
I need to recall it now.

313
00:20:14,671 --> 00:20:18,091
If I don't recall it right this minute,
I'll forget it forever!

314
00:20:18,675 --> 00:20:19,843
Just one thing!

315
00:20:20,928 --> 00:20:22,638
What matters to me?

316
00:20:27,226 --> 00:20:28,227
GO SEE EMPORIO

317
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:32,731
This is all I need.
I'll leave one memory open.

318
00:20:33,273 --> 00:20:34,566
These two things.

319
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:37,819
These two things are all I need.

320
00:20:37,903 --> 00:20:40,280
The rest, I don't need.

321
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:42,699
I need to leave this place!

322
00:20:48,163 --> 00:20:51,208
I spilled… my water.

323
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:55,045
I need to… unplug the power.

324
00:20:55,671 --> 00:20:57,506
The power is shorting out.

325
00:20:58,674 --> 00:21:05,347
Or else, I can't leave out of
that exit to go see Jolyne.

326
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:09,851
I have things I need to tell Jolyne!

327
00:21:10,936 --> 00:21:13,021
I can't forget them!

328
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:16,066
I have to leave this room!

329
00:21:22,614 --> 00:21:24,825
I spilled my water.

330
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:26,827
MEMORY ONE: I SPILLED MY WATER

331
00:21:26,910 --> 00:21:29,037
I need to… unplug the power.

332
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:31,039
MEMORY TWO: I NEED TO UNPLUG THE POWER

333
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:32,749
The power is shorting out.

334
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:34,710
MEMORY THREE: THE POWER IS SHORTING

335
00:21:34,793 --> 00:21:40,424
Or else, I can't leave out of that exit…

336
00:21:41,883 --> 00:21:43,927
MEMORY FOUR: OR ELSE, I CAN'T LEAVE
THIS ROOM TO GO SEE JOLYNE

337
00:21:44,011 --> 00:21:44,845
MEMORY THREE

338
00:21:44,928 --> 00:21:46,430
…to go see Jolyne.

339
00:21:49,266 --> 00:21:50,267
Wait a second.

340
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:52,102
"Go see Emporio"?

341
00:21:53,103 --> 00:21:57,065
I'm sure I read that name on her arm.

342
00:21:57,566 --> 00:21:59,776
I need to go make sure.

343
00:22:00,277 --> 00:22:04,114
No one can escape this place.

344
00:22:04,197 --> 00:22:06,116
GO SEE EMPORIO

345
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:46,299
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
